<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n19288" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλσᾰμ-ον</span></b> , τό, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>balsam-tree, Balsamodendron
				Opobalsamum,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.6.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Dsc.
				1.19
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ξύλα βαλσάμου</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>BGU</u>
					953.6
				</span></i>
			
			<span class="entity">(iii/iv A. D.)</span>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> the fragrant oil of this tree, <i>Mecca balsam,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Fr.</u>
				110
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Thphr.
				<u>HP</u>
				9.4.1
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>POxy.</u>
				1052
			</span></i> (<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βαρσ-,</span>
			<span class="entity">iv A. D.</span>). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>an aromatic herb, costmary, Chrysanthemum Balsamita,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Gp.
				11.27t
			</span></i>it.—Prob. Semitic. [<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">βάλσᾱμον</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Nic.
				<u>Th.</u>
				947
			</span></i>, but <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ᾰ</span> in <i><span class="en">
				Androm.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.39
			</span></i>, and <i><span class="en">
				Damocr.
			</span></i> ap. <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				14.97
			</span></i>, as in <i>balsa^mum</i> in Lat. Poets.]</div>
